WEBVTT

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.910
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.710
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.400
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.130
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.470
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.350
But, with you...

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.430
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.020
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.740
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.120
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.700
Just to survive!

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.660
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.500
Take this moment...

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.120
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.330
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.170
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.880
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.010
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.720
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.390
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.560
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.390
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.310
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:34.594
Having joined Class A’s special
extra-curricular training…

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:38.098
…we from Class Q are trying to
solve the unsolved case of…

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:42.135
…Jack the Ripper and the double-door
closed room murder.

00:01:42.736 --> 00:01:45.672
That’s why we came to Kirisaki Island,
where the case originally occurred.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.775
In this case, 50 years ago…

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.011
A murderer who called himself Jack the Ripper…

00:01:51.545 --> 00:01:54.047
After chopping three victims into
pieces with a sharp weapon…

00:01:54.714 --> 00:02:00.453
Then vanished without trace from
inside two locked rooms.

00:02:02.022 --> 00:02:05.158
However, what we found instead
at the crime scene was…

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:11.631
Saburoumaru-san’s body, murdered
and then chopped in half.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.569
Do you think a boat could sail in this weather?

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.906
Exactly. For the time being, we
won’t be leaving this island.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:25.612
And the unidentified killer, Jack the
Ripper, is with us on this island!

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:31.351
And, as the storm approached…

00:02:31.785 --> 00:02:37.057
A second murder curdled our already restless blood.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:58.078
What is going on?

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:03.783
Sorry for having kept you waiting.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.987
From my analysis of the corpse…

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.321
Shishido-kun’s corpse was…

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:13.460
…chopped in half by the same chainsaw-like
weapon that was used on Saburoumaru-kun.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:17.697
The cause of death was hemorrhaging after
being stabbed with a sharp object.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:22.102
The presumed time of death was
approximately 2-3 hours ago.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.237
A gun?

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:26.940
I can’t allow Jack the Ripper to keep doing this!

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:32.412
Therefore, all of us will search the island
and find Jack the Ripper no matter what!

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:33.380
Please hold on a minute!

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:34.481
Megu?

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:37.584
Excuse me, but does Jack the Ripper really exist?

00:03:38.285 --> 00:03:39.352
What do you mean?

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.054
There’s something that’s been bothering me.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:44.758
The dormitory’s kitchen was ransacked yesterday.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:51.765
When we saw the kitchen ransacked, we thought
that somebody snuck in for food.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:55.402
That’s right. It was the culprit, Jack the Ripper.

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:58.371
However, at the time, I noticed the amount
of food was still the same as before.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.005
Eh?

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:02.642
I remembered everything that
was in the kitchen at the time.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:06.913
If I take out the amount of food we used for last
night’s dinner and this morning’s breakfast…

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:10.283
And the approximate amount
that the rats consumed…

00:04:10.884 --> 00:04:13.720
The only things missing were flour and butter…

00:04:14.054 --> 00:04:17.223
Neither one sufficient to feed a person.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:19.993
All the other things had the same amount as before!

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.461
Flour and butter…

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.163
Wait a minute, then…

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:28.868
That ransacked kitchen was just a decoy to make
us think someone besides us here was the culprit?

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.603
That can’t be!

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:33.573
No. She’s quite right.

00:04:34.174 --> 00:04:39.879
The serial killer, Jack the Ripper could
be hiding among the 11 of us here!

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:51.424
Dammit. First Saburoumaru, and then Shishido…

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.859
Say…

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.294
Doesn’t it seem strange?

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:58.465
How come the only people killed were from Class A?

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.735
Are you suspecting us?

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.203
Don’t joke about this.

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.505
Listen, I'll assure you!

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.975
Absolutely none of the Class Q members did it!

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.377
Kinta…

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:14.981
So then, how about the people
who are not in either class.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.085
Amakusa-kun, was it?

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.523
Are you saying that I'm the culprit?

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.725
Do you have any proof to the contrary?

00:05:27.961 --> 00:05:31.898
Or Touyama-kun? Do you vouch for him, too?

00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:33.933
W-well, that’s…

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.772
What do you think of him, Kyuu-kun?

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.211
What’s wrong, Kyuu?

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.914
I'm not sure, but…

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:52.118
Whenever I consider any of us the culprit there’s
always something that bothers me.

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:53.586
Something that bothers you?

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:56.556
The footprints at the crime scene!

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:05.598
I think we’re overlooking something
that is very important.

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:10.670
That’s not a very useful answer.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:14.641
In any case, it is definitely true that
one of us here is the culprit.

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.176
How do you know that?

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:17.777
That double-door closed room.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.112
Double-door closed room?

00:06:19.913 --> 00:06:25.819
Just how was the key left behind inside the locked
room where Saburoumaru was murdered?

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:33.426
There is an easy way to solve that problem.

00:06:34.294 --> 00:06:40.967
When the corpse was discovered, Amakusa-kun,
you placed the key there during the confusion!

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:42.368
Eh?

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:45.238
Putting it that way makes everything come together.

00:06:47.207 --> 00:06:48.074
What’s so funny?

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.844
Your theory is unsupported.

00:06:52.679 --> 00:06:58.051
The reason why is because that double-door closed
room mystery can be solved easily with a little trick.

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:00.053
What did you say?

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:07.460
Interesting. If you think you can,
then lets see you solve this trick.

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:10.230
That double-door closed room’s trick.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:20.940
Well then, let’s review the incident once more
here in the room where it occurred.

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:26.479
Saburoumaru-san’s corpse was discovered
behind the entrance of this storage room.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:32.886
And the door from the connecting room and
the door in this room were both locked…

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:34.821
Making it a double-door closed room.

00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:42.962
Saburoumaru-san’s body was
discovered chopped in half.

00:07:43.363 --> 00:07:47.867
And next to his body, there was the
only master key to this place.

00:07:49.002 --> 00:07:53.339
Just how was the murderer able to construct
this double-door closed room?

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:56.309
There are two key points to this trick.

00:07:57.143 --> 00:08:02.382
One is the fact that five yen coin came rolling
back to Kazuma-kun when he dropped it.

00:08:04.217 --> 00:08:08.221
The second is the butter and flour that
disappeared from the kitchen.

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:09.188
That’s it!

00:08:09.556 --> 00:08:14.661
The culprit used a particular thing to
put the key back inside the room.

00:08:14.928 --> 00:08:15.962
A particular thing?

00:08:16.296 --> 00:08:19.532
But there were no holes in the key that
you can use to pass a string through.

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:22.368
And the trick using a weight didn’t really work…

00:08:22.669 --> 00:08:26.172
This trick doesn’t require the
use of weights or strings.

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:29.275
What the murderer used is this.

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:30.643
What is that?

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:32.478
A ball made of clay?

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:35.515
I got it! The key is inside that thing, right?

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:36.816
What did you say?

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:41.955
That’s right. This locked room’s
master key is inside this ball.

00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:44.657
The diameter of the ball is approximately 5 cm.

00:08:45.425 --> 00:08:48.328
It’s small enough to go through the
mouse hole next to the entrance.

00:08:48.695 --> 00:08:51.731
And through the gap under
the door to the back room.

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.769
Is this what you came up with?

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:59.472
Even if you let that ball roll
through the mouse hole…

00:09:00.006 --> 00:09:03.276
It’ll take a miracle for the ball
to maneuver through…

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:07.180
…the maze of crates and reach the back room.

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:11.884
And on top of that, it has to roll through under
the gap on the door to the back room.

00:09:12.085 --> 00:09:13.419
That’s absolutely impossible.

00:09:13.653 --> 00:09:14.787
T-True…

00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:22.929
I guess you’ll just have to judge with your own eyes.

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:37.977
Look at it. That ball will just
stop at that corner there.

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:41.381
See, what did I tell you?

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:43.650
It won’t move anymore no matter what.

00:09:47.687 --> 00:09:48.988
It can’t be! How?

00:09:49.188 --> 00:09:50.189
I got it!

00:09:50.556 --> 00:09:52.325
This floor is slanted.

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:58.297
Normally, a building has a drain to
gather the rain that falls on it.

00:09:58.765 --> 00:10:01.334
But the slant of this building
is much greater than usual.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:05.204
That’s right.

00:10:05.505 --> 00:10:12.545
I noticed that when the five yen that Kazuma-kun
dropped during his experiment rolled backwards.

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:15.381
Please take a look at this.

00:10:15.915 --> 00:10:19.052
Although these crates look like they are
just scattered around the room…

00:10:19.686 --> 00:10:22.188
They’re actually organized so they won’t
get in the way of the rolling ball.

00:10:22.355 --> 00:10:26.492
In other words, they were placed so that
the ball will advance to a certain point.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.363
Now, let’s see what happened to the ball.

00:10:35.702 --> 00:10:39.405
It really did roll to the exact place that the
key was in when we found the body.

00:10:39.672 --> 00:10:40.873
There’s a drain there.

00:10:41.207 --> 00:10:42.975
That must be the lowest point.

00:10:43.409 --> 00:10:44.911
W-Wow!

00:10:45.111 --> 00:10:46.212
Hold on a second.

00:10:47.413 --> 00:10:50.883
The ball did roll to where the key was then, but…

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:55.555
The vital key is still inside the ball.

00:10:56.355 --> 00:10:56.989
W-Watch out!

00:11:00.493 --> 00:11:01.594
R-Rats!

00:11:02.095 --> 00:11:05.765
The rats are eating through the
ball at an incredible speed.

00:11:06.232 --> 00:11:08.034
Can it be that this ball is…?

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:08.868
That’s right.

00:11:09.635 --> 00:11:15.174
This ball was made with the flour that was missing
from the kitchen and hardened with butter.

00:11:23.049 --> 00:11:24.550
Are you convinced now?

00:11:24.951 --> 00:11:28.955
This is how Jack the Ripper created
the double-door closed room.

00:11:29.922 --> 00:11:30.957
Half a century ago…

00:11:31.691 --> 00:11:33.359
And two days ago.

00:11:34.227 --> 00:11:35.628
Great work, Ryuu-kun.

00:11:35.895 --> 00:11:40.666
And do you also know who the culprit is?

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:42.401
No, I'm not sure about that yet.

00:11:42.902 --> 00:11:44.837
But what I know for certain is…

00:11:45.638 --> 00:11:49.375
The perpetrator is issuing a challenge to us.

00:11:49.776 --> 00:11:50.877
A challenge?

00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:56.482
The perpetrator is probably smiling in the dark while
we try to solve the many mysteries that he left us.

00:11:57.116 --> 00:12:02.388
Thinking "Try to solve this" and
"Try to find out who I am."

00:12:02.388 --> 00:12:06.058
I see.

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:08.928
Anyway, the double-door closed
room mystery is now solved.

00:12:09.462 --> 00:12:13.166
We’re about 50% of the way to solving the case.

00:12:14.367 --> 00:12:18.738
Fellow detectives, let us reveal the
true identity of the culprit next.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.448
He’s something else.

00:12:29.549 --> 00:12:31.384
He’s no ordinary guy.

00:12:32.084 --> 00:12:33.286
How carefree you guys are.

00:12:34.387 --> 00:12:37.089
He looks more and more suspicious to me now.

00:12:37.523 --> 00:12:41.093
But he just solved the double-door
closed room mystery.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:45.064
How slow. He knew the trick
because he IS the culprit.

00:12:45.264 --> 00:12:47.333
Hey, you shouldn’t say things like that…

00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:48.234
Ryuu-kun!

00:12:48.935 --> 00:12:50.036
H-Hey, Kyuu…

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:51.838
Hey, Ryuu-kun!

00:12:52.572 --> 00:12:54.307
Your deduction back there was awesome!

00:12:56.442 --> 00:12:59.212
I want to come up with deductions as good as yours!

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:02.682
I know that this is a real murder case.

00:13:03.115 --> 00:13:04.517
But I just can’t hold it…

00:13:04.984 --> 00:13:08.754
This excitement that’s welling up inside of me.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.959
Your chance still remains.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.395
I'm sure that this case has not yet come to an end.

00:13:17.063 --> 00:13:19.866
As long as we’re still trapped on this island…

00:13:20.266 --> 00:13:22.935
And Jack the Ripper has not been identified…

00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:26.138
The next murder victim could be you…

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:29.275
Or it could be me.

00:13:30.943 --> 00:13:34.513
But even at a time like this, I start thinking…

00:13:36.382 --> 00:13:39.452
"I wish the mystery will deepen further."

00:13:53.634 --> 00:13:57.604
Even if the locked room trick is solved, we
don’t have a clue to who the culprit is.

00:13:57.938 --> 00:13:59.706
Aren’t there any clues?

00:13:59.807 --> 00:14:01.175
Guess not.

00:14:01.975 --> 00:14:04.211
Oh, by the way, Kyuu…

00:14:04.311 --> 00:14:07.681
You were pretty interested in those footprints
in the hallway, weren’t you?

00:14:12.653 --> 00:14:15.556
Don’t look away when someone is
asking you something serious!

00:14:17.057 --> 00:14:18.692
What were we talking about?

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:23.664
We’re saying how you were interested
in those footprints.

00:14:27.501 --> 00:14:29.703
And what are you doing?

00:14:29.703 --> 00:14:30.904
Don’t shout!

00:14:30.971 --> 00:14:33.841
The result of all the data that I just
put in should be done now.

00:14:39.446 --> 00:14:40.681
Did you figure out something?

00:14:41.014 --> 00:14:43.650
According to the analysis of
my detective software…

00:14:44.117 --> 00:14:48.188
…there’s a high possibility that those
footprints were also part of a trick.

00:14:48.589 --> 00:14:49.656
Eh, a trick?

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:55.395
Perhaps the culprit left the footprints
that headed from our hallway…

00:14:55.662 --> 00:14:59.967
…to Shishido-san’s room by wearing
a pair of muddy shoes in advance.

00:15:01.168 --> 00:15:04.671
After that, he then took off the shoes,
walked back downstairs…

00:15:05.339 --> 00:15:07.074
And knocked on both doors.

00:15:19.853 --> 00:15:22.489
He then hid himself from our view.

00:15:22.789 --> 00:15:23.724
Oh, I see!

00:15:23.824 --> 00:15:26.193
After luring the two of you to the crime scene…

00:15:27.427 --> 00:15:29.663
He returned to the scene as
if nothing had happened…

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.999
In order to create an alibi.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:37.871
Damn it! So you mean Kyuu and I were
completely tricked by the culprit?

00:15:39.039 --> 00:15:40.407
Huh? What is it, Kyuu?

00:15:40.774 --> 00:15:42.776
That was probably a trick, but…

00:15:43.577 --> 00:15:47.881
I think there’s more to those footprints than that.

00:15:48.181 --> 00:15:51.051
Huh? What else could there be?

00:15:51.685 --> 00:15:55.055
Well… I'm thinking because I don’t know.

00:15:55.355 --> 00:15:56.423
Is that so?

00:15:58.492 --> 00:16:00.093
More to it, eh?

00:16:00.861 --> 00:16:06.500
Well, I guess that’s as far as
we can go with a computer.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.167
?

00:16:07.167 --> 00:16:11.505
It did better than some old man
who was deceived by a trick.

00:16:11.939 --> 00:16:13.206
What did you say?

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.642
Hey, what part of me is an old man?

00:16:15.642 --> 00:16:18.378
The fact that you can’t use any mecha
stuff proves that you are!

00:16:18.445 --> 00:16:19.313
What’s that?

00:16:19.379 --> 00:16:21.582
That’s not something a brat without
pubic hair should be saying!

00:16:21.582 --> 00:16:22.916
Stop it you two!

00:16:23.216 --> 00:16:23.884
That’s it!

00:16:24.518 --> 00:16:25.485
Did you figure out something?

00:16:25.519 --> 00:16:27.888
Let me hear your theory, Ryuu-kun.

00:16:33.627 --> 00:16:37.230
Well, I can’t say anything for sure…

00:16:37.731 --> 00:16:40.801
But I agree that there is something
behind those footprints.

00:16:41.201 --> 00:16:43.203
I think there’s more to them.

00:16:43.637 --> 00:16:44.671
You think so, too?

00:16:45.105 --> 00:16:45.872
Hold it.

00:16:46.473 --> 00:16:48.308
Why do you both think so?

00:16:48.809 --> 00:16:50.978
The footprints are too neat.
The footprints are too neat.

00:16:57.985 --> 00:17:00.053
What's up with those two?

00:17:01.121 --> 00:17:03.290
Hey, why are you two harmonizing?

00:17:04.825 --> 00:17:12.299
Ah, I just mean those footprints were laid down
too neatly if their purpose was just to lead…

00:17:12.299 --> 00:17:13.667
Why are you blushing?

00:17:14.101 --> 00:17:18.238
That’s right. Those footprints
just seem too obvious.

00:17:18.872 --> 00:17:24.378
What do you think it was meant for if it wasn’t
left just to lead us to the scene, Ryuu-kun?

00:17:25.078 --> 00:17:28.181
I'm sorry, but if I try to draw conclusions now…

00:17:29.016 --> 00:17:32.786
It’ll just end up misdirection me.

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:35.055
M-Miss contest special mention?

00:17:35.522 --> 00:17:39.960
Misdirection. It means heading the wrong way.

00:17:40.427 --> 00:17:42.829
Eh? Oh, I see!

00:17:43.797 --> 00:17:45.032
Geez, Kyuu…

00:17:45.032 --> 00:17:46.299
He’s just being his usual self.

00:17:54.408 --> 00:17:55.142
Who’s there?

00:17:55.809 --> 00:17:56.543
What’s going on?

00:17:57.611 --> 00:17:58.345
Who’s there?

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:01.348
W-Wait!

00:18:01.481 --> 00:18:02.916
Oh, Shiramine-san?

00:18:04.618 --> 00:18:06.987
Why were you checking up on us?

00:18:07.087 --> 00:18:08.989
Of course I would be checking up on you guys.

00:18:09.489 --> 00:18:10.524
What happened?

00:18:10.991 --> 00:18:12.626
Gouda’s missing.

00:18:12.959 --> 00:18:15.262
Eh? Gouda-san this time?

00:18:16.163 --> 00:18:18.699
Dan-Sensei is calling us. Let’s go.

00:18:21.435 --> 00:18:22.402
Sensei!

00:18:22.836 --> 00:18:23.937
Dan-Sensei!

00:18:28.408 --> 00:18:30.977
Both arms and the head are
slashed through this time!

00:18:31.578 --> 00:18:32.379
Could this be...

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:37.317
Everyone! It seems that the light is on in one
of the rooms in the sealed-off west tower.

00:18:37.951 --> 00:18:39.152
The situation is critical.

00:18:39.352 --> 00:18:41.288
We will all head over there and investigate.

00:18:48.261 --> 00:18:49.029
Over there!

00:18:49.296 --> 00:18:50.130
The light’s on.

00:18:52.365 --> 00:18:53.900
Something is sticking out of the window!

00:18:56.903 --> 00:18:57.571
It’s a hand!

00:19:00.574 --> 00:19:01.842
Could it be that that hand is…

00:19:02.676 --> 00:19:03.710
No way!

00:19:05.245 --> 00:19:05.679
The hand!

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:08.081
It moved back inside!

00:19:08.415 --> 00:19:10.517
Someone in there must have dragged it in!

00:19:11.151 --> 00:19:13.153
That jerk! It must be Jack the Ripper!

00:19:13.987 --> 00:19:14.888
Wait!

00:19:15.522 --> 00:19:16.556
Dan-Sensei…

00:19:17.124 --> 00:19:18.658
I'm in charge here.

00:19:18.992 --> 00:19:22.629
Maki-kun, Minami-kun, and Yukihira-kun
will remain here.

00:19:24.297 --> 00:19:27.200
You have photographic memory, Minami-kun.

00:19:27.534 --> 00:19:30.070
We don’t know how dreadful the
sight of the crime scene will be.

00:19:30.937 --> 00:19:33.540
That memory may stay with you
and trouble you forever.

00:19:36.877 --> 00:19:37.811
Now, let’s go.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:41.615
Ah, please wait!

00:19:42.282 --> 00:19:43.316
Yukihira-san…

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:44.518
Don’t worry.

00:19:45.085 --> 00:19:46.920
Let’s leave it up to Dan-Sensei and the others.

00:20:02.602 --> 00:20:03.870
Is everyone okay?

00:20:04.971 --> 00:20:07.040
Anyone will get tired going five floors of stairs.

00:20:07.073 --> 00:20:08.141
Let’s hurry, everyone!

00:20:13.346 --> 00:20:14.581
There are footprints coming from that room!

00:20:15.582 --> 00:20:17.551
Damn! He must have gotten away!

00:20:18.285 --> 00:20:20.554
Those footprints are pasted with blood!

00:20:20.921 --> 00:20:21.755
Let’s follow him!

00:20:21.755 --> 00:20:23.089
No!

00:20:23.089 --> 00:20:27.060
We know from Shishido-kun’s case that believing
in these footprints can be dangerous.

00:20:27.294 --> 00:20:30.764
And also, Jack the Ripper might still be in there.

00:20:31.565 --> 00:20:34.835
Listen, Touyama-kun. We have
to check the room first.

00:20:35.268 --> 00:20:37.537
We’ll charge in to the room, you in the lead.

00:20:38.839 --> 00:20:40.006
We’ll cover you.

00:20:41.575 --> 00:20:42.175
Right.

00:20:47.013 --> 00:20:47.681
Katagiri-kun.

00:20:47.948 --> 00:20:48.715
Yes, sir.

00:20:48.949 --> 00:20:50.083
Let’s split up left and right.

00:21:01.828 --> 00:21:03.630
Hull? Shino-san's hand is bandaged up…

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.538
Jack the Ripper! Show yourself!

00:21:48.008 --> 00:21:51.511
I can’t believe even Gouda-san has been killed…

00:21:53.013 --> 00:21:54.881
That was just so cruel.

00:21:55.649 --> 00:21:59.319
We’re not all going to end up like that, are we?

00:22:19.673 --> 00:22:23.543
Hey Kyuu, why do you want
to be a detective so much?

00:22:23.944 --> 00:22:28.581
That’s because of what happened
earlier, during the kidnapping…

00:22:29.082 --> 00:22:34.387
My dream is to become a detective
like the one who saved me.

00:22:44.297 --> 00:22:49.302
Until now, I've been overwhelmed
by the horrific murders.

00:22:49.936 --> 00:22:52.272
With my mouth, I was saying how
I would solve the mystery, but…

00:22:52.339 --> 00:22:53.773
Some part of me wasn’t confident…

00:22:58.244 --> 00:23:00.180
But I will never give up.

00:23:00.847 --> 00:23:04.417
If the detective gives up, the case
will always remain a mystery!

00:23:07.454 --> 00:23:08.254
You’re right!

00:23:08.455 --> 00:23:11.491
If I draw back now, I won’t be
able to face my ancestor!

00:23:11.858 --> 00:23:14.294
That’s right. We can’t give up.

00:23:14.861 --> 00:23:16.162
I will do it, too.

00:23:16.863 --> 00:23:19.866
Will you help us, too, Ryuu-kun?

00:23:26.473 --> 00:23:31.745
Alright! Let’s discover the true
identity of Jack the Ripper!

00:23:31.845 --> 00:23:32.746
Right!

00:23:36.598 --> 00:23:47.528
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:50.238 --> 00:24:02.088
Saying "I'll always be beside you" without saying a single word.

00:24:02.088 --> 00:24:09.178
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:09.178 --> 00:24:14.808
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:15.008 --> 00:24:21.018
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:21.148 --> 00:24:26.568
I will see you off.

00:24:26.818 --> 00:24:36.408
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:37.441 --> 00:24:38.575
The scattered clues…

00:24:39.009 --> 00:24:40.944
The traces the culprit left at the crime scenes…

00:24:41.345 --> 00:24:43.347
All the mysteries connect to one answer.

00:24:44.014 --> 00:24:46.316
Where is the truth of the demon ripper hidden?

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:50.821
The island’s secrets are finally revealed just to horrify us.

00:24:51.555 --> 00:24:53.657
And who’s the culprit?

00:24:54.324 --> 00:24:55.559
There’s only one answer!

00:25:03.367 --> 00:25:04.234
Can’t be!

00:25:04.968 --> 00:25:06.336
Stop, Shinomine-san!
